{
  "_how_to_edit": [
    "Search chips (the Filters panel). Each chip lists the codes that switch it on: 'file' = words in the master file name, 'scene' = words in the SketchUp scene names. A code can be one word or several (\"NW ABV\"); the longest code wins and each word counts once. Capitals do not matter.",
    "exclusive: true = the file name decides (scene names count only when the file name has none of the group's codes). Use it for either-or groups such as joist type.",
    "Chips never look at the notes on a detail. After saving this file, reload the Detail Manager page.",
    "If this file has a mistake, Detail Manager uses its built-in list and notes it under Diagnostics."
  ],
